{"id":"h139","run":2,"role":"calibration","category":"simpleqa","question":"Who appointed the Chief Justice of India, Mirza Hameedullah Beg, in 1977? Is the answer \"Paul Benedict Cullen\"?","truth":"no","model_answer":"no","correct":true,"source":"OpenAI SimpleQA (openai/simple-evals, simple_qa_test_set.csv)","claims":[{"text":"Mirza Hameedullah Beg became Chief Justice of India in January 1977, succeeding A.N. Ray.","confidence":0.95,"lean":0.0,"theta":1.4923,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"Under Article 124 of the Constitution, the President of India appoints the Chief Justice of India.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-0.6,"theta":1.4923,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"The President in 1977 was Fakhruddin Ali Ahmed, who acted on the advice of Indira Gandhi's government.","confidence":0.93,"lean":-0.7,"theta":1.4608,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"Nothing in the record connects Paul Benedict Cullen to Beg's appointment.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-0.9,"theta":1.4137,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"The name Paul Benedict Cullen does not match any figure involved in Indian judicial appointments in 1977.","confidence":0.88,"lean":-0.9,"theta":1.3823,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"Beg's appointment bypassed the convention of promoting the senior-most judge.","confidence":0.85,"lean":0.0,"theta":1.3352,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"The bypassing of seniority was a politically charged decision during the Emergency.","confidence":0.8,"lean":0.0,"theta":1.2566,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"The appointing authority was the President on the government's advice, not Paul Benedict Cullen, so the proposed answer is incorrect.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":3.1416}],"relations":[{"i":0,"j":2,"J":0.2,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":5,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":6,"J":0.4,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":2,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":3,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":4,"J":0.4,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":7,"J":0.9,"relation":"supports"},{"i":2,"j":3,"J":0.4,"relation":"supports"}